The `asyncGeneratorToReadableStream` function lacks error handling. If `gen.next()` throws an error or the generator encounters an error, the `controller.error(error)` should be called to propagate the error to the stream consumer. Without this, errors may be silently swallowed or cause unhandled promise rejections.

```suggestion
export function asyncGeneratorToReadableStream<T>(gen: AsyncGenerator<T>): ReadableStream<T> {
  return new ReadableStream<T>({
    async pull(controller) {
      try {
        const { value, done } = await gen.next()
        if (done) {
          controller.close()
        } else {
          controller.enqueue(value)
        }
      } catch (error) {
        controller.error(error)
      }
    },
    cancel() {
      gen.return?.()
    }
  })
}
```

